ZR-005 — EFFECTIVE SEMANTIC SNAPSHOT / INACTIVE-LINEAGE ISOLATION
Severity: HIGH

Current-source problem:
The final files have correct high-level "COMPLETE CROSS-REVIEWED WORKING CANDIDATE / SEMANTIC REVIEW COMPLETE" front matter, but immediately retain staged/historical review prose that says branches are unresolved or promotion is blocked.
Append-only precedence can theoretically resolve this, but a new human or parser can encounter contradictory release states before reaching later addenda.

Proposed repair:
Generate a hash-bound EffectiveSemanticSnapshot / ActiveDefinitionIndex at the top of each release:
- active semantic owner for each anchor/current package;
- effective status/version/source range;
- superseded/inactive lineage refs;
- active unresolved/deferred items;
- release-level assurance states.
Retained staged candidate/review material is explicitly HISTORICAL/INACTIVE and cannot override the snapshot.
Do not delete lineage.

