ZR-006 — NORMATIVE/EVIDENCE SEPARATION FOR REVIEW-PACKET BINDINGS
Severity: HIGH

Current V159 reviewed-packet binding blocks state that cited packet synthesis/evidence is "part of the semantic reading" of a layer.
Annexure release closure also expects CurrentReadingMap and UpgradeTraceabilityTable/manifest bindings.

Problem:
A final semantic source should not require external reviewer packet content to know its normative meaning. Review packet hashes are evidence lineage, not semantic authority. User-facing final release can also become non-self-contained if required support artifacts are absent.

Proposed repair:
- Review packets, model outputs, hashes and review IDs are TRACEABILITY_EVIDENCE_ONLY.
- Every admitted semantic delta MUST be materialized in normative final source bytes under an explicit active owner/anchor.
- CurrentReadingMap / UpgradeTraceability / ReleaseManifest required to interpret a release must be embedded or bundled as first-class release artifacts and hash-bound.
- Missing review evidence may affect assurance/release validation, but cannot silently supply normative semantics absent from source.

