ZR-007 — SINGLE-OWNER CROSS-LAYER OVERLAY PROJECTION
Severity: MEDIUM

Current final files contain a byte-identical P038-P042 cross-layer overlay tail in all five layers.

Problem:
Repeated normative copies increase size and create future divergence risk; all copies must remain byte-identical forever.

Proposed repair:
- One normative cross-layer current-reading overlay owner (prefer Annexure/release registry or an explicit sixth release artifact).
- Each layer gets only its applicable projection plus hash/reference to the normative overlay.
- Layer-specific material semantics remain in their proper owner.
- Existing retained copies may remain lineage/inactive; future active releases stop multiplying the same normative block.

