ZR-009 — MACHINE-BINDING CLOSURE LEDGER / RELEASE-STATUS SPLIT
Severity: HIGH

Current Technical T-EH-01..T-EH-20 each explicitly say machine binding UNRESOLVED, with machine_contract_id/version null and status UNRESOLVED_REQUIRED_BEFORE_EXECUTABLE_ADMISSION.
The release also correctly says NOT EXECUTABLY CERTIFIED.

Problem:
"SEMANTIC REVIEW COMPLETE" can still be misread as broader closure, and unresolved machine bindings are scattered rather than summarized as a release-level closure dimension.

Proposed repair:
- Preserve the EH semantic profiles; do NOT invent machine IDs.
- Release assurance surface explicitly carries:
  DESIGN_SEMANTIC_REVIEW = COMPLETE_WITHIN_DECLARED_SCOPE
  MACHINE_BINDING_CLOSURE = INCOMPLETE
  EXECUTED_CONFORMANCE = NOT_CLAIMED/INCOMPLETE
  EMPIRICAL_VALIDATION = owner-qualified
  EXTERNAL_CERTIFICATION = NOT_CLAIMED
- Add a MachineBindingClosureLedger for T-EH-01..20 binding expected owner, function/result algebra/resource/termination semantics, current binding state, required tests and blockers.
- Executable admission cannot occur while required binding entries remain unresolved.

