ZR-010 — TYPED THEORY RELEASE REGISTRY
Severity: MEDIUM

Current source already has TheoryArtifact, TheoryApplicabilityResult, theory registries and individual prose classifications.
But the Theories layer presents heterogeneous items under a broad "theory" umbrella:
SRT modeling/ontology framework; VSM persistent-state theory; RPM/PPM control/regulation frameworks; TFT transport framework; FET safety-reflex architecture; SCT epistemic governance architecture; plus Reference Architectures and research profiles.
The release also refines some theories without making current effective version/status obvious near the top.

Proposed repair:
Extend the existing TheoryArtifact/current theory registry metadata (do not create a new Engine) with fields equivalent to:
- artifact_kind / semantic_role
- current_effective_semantic_version
- release_effective_status
- validation_mode/evidence class
- supersedes/refines lineage
- current owner/source anchor
- applicability/falsifiers
Add a Theory Release Registry near the top of Theories that distinguishes modeling ontology/state/control/effective-domain/safety architecture/epistemic governance/reference architecture/research profile (exact enum names challengeable).
Goal: the expected proof/validation burden is type-visible and release versioning is unambiguous.

