ZR-011 — PROFILE-BIND REFERENCE-ARCHITECTURE OPERATIONAL CONSTANTS
Severity: MEDIUM

Current [RA-RELIABILITY-OS] "Full Specification" contains fixed operational values such as:
- evaluation coverage alert <0.8; cold-start 0.60
- availability/error/latency incident thresholds
- 2-minute degrade / 10-minute recover windows
- max 3 retries
Other reference profiles contain consensus cardinalities and timing thresholds.
The current source already labels performance percentages as illustrative/unvalidated, but operational control constants are not uniformly marked as reference defaults/profile parameters.

Proposed repair:
Every reference-architecture operational numeric constant must be one of:
A) bound to a versioned qualified parameter/profile with scope/evidence; or
B) explicitly tagged ILLUSTRATIVE_REFERENCE_DEFAULT / NON-NORMATIVE.
No reference-architecture default silently becomes a universal Garden invariant.
Domain-qualified safety limits that are already bound to an admitted safety case/profile remain valid.

===============================================================================
ZR-012 — ANCHOR DECLARATION COHERENCE / ATOMIC CHILD-UNIT INDEX
Severity: MEDIUM

Current source uses mixed declaration styles:
- SemanticAnchor: [X]
- inline [X] headings
- V159 package headings
- backlinks that repeat anchor tokens
Some anchors are contentless adjacent declarations (for example T-V155; RA-GSL-KR/RA-GSL-AR/RA-TRAIN appear as adjacent/grouped reference declarations before content).
Some anchor blocks are very large and contain many independent subtopics.

Proposed repair:
- Every active semantic definition has exactly one machine-readable DefinitionRecord: anchor ID, layer, owner, effective source range/hash, status, parent/child relation and aliases.
- A contentless anchor must be explicit ALIAS_OF/GROUP_REF; parser cannot infer ownership from adjacency.
- Backlinks are typed references, never competing definitions.
- Very large active units receive child-unit IDs/source ranges so atomic review/change-impact analysis is deterministic.
- Do not change semantic meaning merely to satisfy formatting.

